    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The \"hope for the dead\"... that's a strange thing to seek. Is there truly anything left for a man like me but to join them? Even the gods have turned their backs on these ruins. I look at my sword, and it's the only thing that feels real anymore. It's the only thing that doesn't lie to me about the darkness. It just waits. Does a story even need to have a hero anymore, or is it more poetic to just let it fade into the shadows?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
